Subject: [PATCH 2/5] feat(sync): newest-first full-sync walk (latest year
 lands first)

Full sync now plans chunked windows from today BACKWARDS to the extraction
start. The checkpoint frontier is LastFromDate (oldest date extracted),
marked with LastAlterId=2; interruptions resume going further back, so the
most recent data is always in BigQuery first. Legacy forward checkpoints
are detected and the walk restarts (idempotent batch IDs absorb overlap).
Timed-out windows split newer-half-first during the walk; forward
incremental keeps chronological split order.

